  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "9466098",
      "title": "Understanding Margin Collapsing and Removing Default Margins",
      "lectureOrder": 28,
      "videoOrder": 23,
      "sourceHash": "77ecda9a425597b79c334ff33bd2c0e5e888d0dc0d3bb22e00742393dab085a0",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.27,
          "end": 8.96,
          "en": "We had a look at the box model basics with padding, a border and a margin and all these things are of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 8.96,
          "end": 9.79,
          "en": "course optional.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.8,
          "end": 12.34,
          "en": "You can get a padding and a margin without a border,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.35,
          "end": 16.97,
          "en": "you can have a border without a padding and margin, so that's all totally optional",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 17.24,
          "end": 18.75,
          "en": "and it leads to that result.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.81,
          "end": 21.98,
          "en": "Now I mentioned there would be a couple of special things,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.98,
          "end": 25.9,
          "en": "now let's dive into these special things step-by-step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.03,
          "end": 29.78,
          "en": "The first special thing can be seen if you inspect the section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.9,
          "end": 36.62,
          "en": "There is some whitespace to the left and to the right, so after the orange margin, this is coming from",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 36.62,
          "end": 37.81,
          "en": "the body actually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 37.94,
          "end": 43.65,
          "en": "If you hover over the body, you can see the body also has a default margin, here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 43.69,
          "end": 44.96,
          "en": "the 8 pixels,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 45.17,
          "end": 49.12,
          "en": "that is simply coming from the browser defaults here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 49.13,
          "end": 56.27,
          "en": "So what we can do to help prevent this and to make sure that our elements go directly into the edges",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 56.42,
          "end": 57.54,
          "en": "of our page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 57.74,
          "end": 61.96,
          "en": "we can set that margin to zero with that margin zero command.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 62.27,
          "end": 67.42,
          "en": "If we do that and we reload the page, you see now the body has no longer a margin",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 67.55,
          "end": 73.28999999999999,
          "en": "and therefore if we inspect the section, you indeed see the orange area around it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 73.4,
          "end": 79.43,
          "en": "so its margin directly connects to the edges of the page which means there is no additional space in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 79.43,
          "end": 80.17,
          "en": "between.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 80.45,
          "end": 87.92,
          "en": "So that was the first special thing, that the body has a margin. Another special thing can be seen if we inspect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 88.01,
          "end": 92.47999999999999,
          "en": "the h1 tag in our second section, in the plans section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 92.47999999999999,
          "end": 98.72,
          "en": "You see, this has a margin to the top and bottom, the default margin every h1 element has, we can",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 98.72,
          "end": 100.58,
          "en": "see here, it's orange.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 100.58,
          "end": 105.75,
          "en": "Now the interesting thing is if we also inspect the section above it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 105.75,
          "end": 107.86,
          "en": "so the product overview section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 108.18,
          "end": 111.77000000000001,
          "en": "do you see that orange margin at the bottom of it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 111.78,
          "end": 113.27000000000001,
          "en": "Keep in mind where it was.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 113.52000000000001,
          "end": 120.76,
          "en": "If I go back to the h1 tag, it overlaps with that section from the product overview container.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 121.09,
          "end": 124.54,
          "en": "This behavior is called margin collapsing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 124.77,
          "end": 126.32,
          "en": "it simply means the following,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 126.51,
          "end": 132.16,
          "en": "if you got two elements block element with its box model, the margin is the orange part here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 132.38,
          "end": 139.1,
          "en": "if you got two elements next to each other, then margins between them are actually collapsed to one margin,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 139.14,
          "end": 140.93,
          "en": "the bigger margin wins.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 141.21,
          "end": 142.34,
          "en": "This is not a bug,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 142.41,
          "end": 143.77,
          "en": "this is on purpose.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 143.79,
          "end": 152.94,
          "en": "This is there or this is enforced by CSS to ensure that you don't get two big distances between the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 152.94,
          "end": 153.88,
          "en": "elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 153.92000000000002,
          "end": 156.57,
          "en": "Now you could argue, hey leave that up to me,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 156.63,
          "end": 157.79,
          "en": "I'll take care of that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 157.98,
          "end": 159.98,
          "en": "but that's simply not how CSS works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 159.99,
          "end": 163.39,
          "en": "so it is something to be aware of. To work around this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 163.41,
          "end": 169.98,
          "en": "it's a good practice to use either margin top or margin bottom unless you don't worry about this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 169.99,
          "end": 173.18,
          "en": "collapsing occurring which of course also can be the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 173.18,
          "end": 177.66,
          "en": "So in our case, we got some collapsing, it's not really a problem because we've got a fine distance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 177.66,
          "end": 179.23,
          "en": "between the elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 179.25,
          "end": 183.27,
          "en": "I just want to highlight it here so that you don't wonder what's going on here.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
